==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|evident|ly|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈɛvɪdəntli/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-evidently.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# {{label|en|obsolete}}&nbsp; In such a way as to be clearly [[visible]] or [[manifest]]; [[distinctly]], [[clearly]]. {{defdate|14th-19th c.}}
#* '''1526''', {{w|William Tyndale}}, trans. ''Bible'', Acts X:
#*: The same man sawe in a vysion '''evydently''' aboute the nynthe houre of the daye the angell of god commynge in unto hym [...].
# In a manner which makes the fact or conclusion [[evident]]; [[obviously]], as may be clearly inferred. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#* {{quote-book|year=1963|author={{w|Margery Allingham}}
|title={{w|The China Governess}}
|chapter=1|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL2004261W
|passage=The half-dozen pieces […] were painted white and carved with festoons of flowers, birds and cupids. To display them the walls had been tinted a vivid blue which had now faded, but the carpet, which had '''evidently''' been stored and recently relaid, retained its original turquoise.}}

